The structure should be as open to change as [http://www.interseo.com the content], though once there's a large structure, we'll need a site map, table of contents, and topic pages to organize it all. Changing the structure at that point will require more work. That said, if you reorganize things, do your best to avoid orphaning somebody's work. Make sure every page that used to be available via a link is <i>still</i> available.

Respect your fellow wiki maintainers. If [http://www.sba.com.cn somebody] gets something wrong, like "2 + 2 = 5", go ahead and correct it, but matters of opinion are just that. If you disagree, put a link in the other person's piece to your rejoinder on a new page (or use the TitleTalk convention).

